{"availability":"available","full":"glortho/react-keydown","name":"react-keydown","description":"Lightweight keydown wrapper for React components","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":495,"forks":34,"created":"2015-10-02T16:16:39Z","updated":"2026-07-16T19:43:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"http://glortho.github.io/react-keydown/example/index.html","topics":[],"demo":"http://glortho.github.io/react-keydown/example/index.html","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:00.881Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:00.881Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:00.881Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:07.736Z","stars":495,"forks":34},{"at":"2026-10-08T00:28:10.298Z","stars":495,"forks":34},{"at":"2026-10-10T03:22:00.881Z","stars":495,"forks":34}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Use react-keydown as a higher-order component or decorator to pass keydown events to the wrapped component, or call methods directly via designated keys. Good for implementing keyboard navigation or other shortcuts.","Consult the API & Reference Documentation or continue reading below for quick start.","NOTE: react-keydown doesn't use decorators itself, but to use the @keydown pattern in your application you will need a transpiler like Babel and a decorator transform plugin like this:"],"features":["Declarative syntax: Components say what keys they will respond to.","Intuitive DX: Decorate a class or method to bind it to specified keys.","Scoping: Designate the scope of your bindings by decorating/wrapping components. Only those components and their children will receive the designated key events, and then only when they appear to be active.","Modifier keys: Support for standard modifier key combinations.","Lightweight: 2kb compressed and gzipped, and only attaches a single keydown listener to document, no matter how many keybindings you specify."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/glortho/react-keydown/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"308ccf7d7000750916a3c01e1912cf0e4794fd3a6d168ccdc1e2b252a183ee06","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:07.850Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:07.850Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Use react-keydown as a higher-order component or decorator to pass keydown events to the wrapped component, or call methods directly via designated keys. Good for implementing keyboard navigation or other shortcuts.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/glortho/react-keydown/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"308ccf7d7000750916a3c01e1912cf0e4794fd3a6d168ccdc1e2b252a183ee06","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/glortho/react-keydown/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:07.851Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-16T19:43:23Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/glortho/react-keydown/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:07.851Z","hash":"308ccf7d7000750916a3c01e1912cf0e4794fd3a6d168ccdc1e2b252a183ee06","originalBytes":8315,"storedBytes":8315,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["keydown","keys","component","class","only","react-keydown","event","key","method","methods","enter","events","components","extends","import","javascript","keydownscoped","react.component","decorator","mycomponent","specify","work","decorate","default","input","other","printable","react","should","support","their","when","binding","bindings","both","context","decorated","decorators","get","handling","higher-order","inspect","keydown.event","multiple","note","npm","passed","receive","render","return","since","submit","where","active.","amd","argument","babel","been","bind","branch","build","case","child","classes","clicked","codes","commonjs","componentwillreceiveprops","console.log","const","context.","could","demo","designated","directly","down","else","example","focused","good","handle","here","install","instance","instead.","just","keybind